# Atellar conventions

## Style

- Minimal, solid Go. Do not split files or add abstractions without a reason.
- Match existing naming and patterns. Read a file before editing it.
- Docs and code comments are English. No em-dashes in docs or comments.
- Every feature ships with tests. Prefer table driven tests.

## Layout

Only `cmd/` and `pkg/` at the top level.

```
cmd/atellar                 the single atellar binary
cmd/atellar/internal/cli    cobra commands
cmd/atellar/internal/server API server process (atellar server run)
cmd/atellar/internal/agent  node agent process (atellar agent run)
cmd/atellar/internal/workload  container lifecycle on a node
cmd/atellar/internal/host   files and systemd units for install commands
pkg/api                     api.Interface, errors, watch
pkg/apis/core/v1            API types and validation
pkg/apiserver               api.Interface implementation (authz, scheduling, IPAM)
pkg/transport               HTTP and gRPC servers and clients (TCP is a stub)
pkg/storage                 storage.Interface, memory and postgres stores
pkg/network                 ipam, overlay (VXLAN), netns
pkg/client, pkg/client/informer, pkg/controller, pkg/config, pkg/auth
```

No domain/usecase/port layering and no CRDs.

## CLI

There is one binary, `atellar`. Do not add other binaries.

```
atellar server install|run
atellar node install|join|renew-key|trust-ca
atellar agent run
atellar config set-cluster|set-context|use-context|current-context|get-contexts
atellar nodes list|get|evict|overlay-ips|watch
atellar containers list|get|create|delete|events|watch
atellar join-tokens list|create
atellar version
```

## API

- `api.Interface` is defined once in `pkg/api`. Every transport carries all of it.
- Errors are `*api.Error` with a `Reason`; transports map reasons to status codes and back.
- Watches send ADDED for the snapshot, one BOOKMARK, then changes.
- Authorization lives in `pkg/apiserver`; `apiservertest.Cases()` must list every method.

## Fixed paths

| Path | Use |
|------|-----|
| `/usr/local/bin/atellar` | binary |
| `/etc/atellar/api.env` | API server environment |
| `/usr/share/atellar/migrations` | SQL migrations |
| `/etc/atellar/pki` | cluster CA and API server certificate |
| `/etc/atellar/agent.json` | agent configuration |
| `/var/log/atellar` | container logs |
| `~/.atellar/config` | CLI contexts |

Keep `docs/` aligned with these rules when changing the CLI, API or layout.
